status PROPOSED
status STANDING
status REVISED
status RETRACTED
status SUPERSEDED
status DORMANT
  detail Designed, unimplemented, not contradicted. Absence from recent work is not evidence against it.

verification_state VERIFIED_ON_DISK
  detail Something in the working estate confirms it.
verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT
  detail A measurement over a named universe confirms it.
verification_state ASSERTED_FROM_DOCUMENT
  detail Stated in a design artifact; not independently checked.
verification_state ASSERTED_BY_INFERENCE
  detail Concluded from adjacent evidence rather than direct observation. The weakest state and the one that produced this session's two retractions.
verification_state CONTRADICTED

lineage_field claim
lineage_field ancestors
lineage_field descendants
lineage_field surviving_invariants
lineage_field invalidated_assumptions
lineage_field realized_bindings
lineage_field current_evidence

correction_rule a retraction records what was claimed, what was checked, what was found and what the claim becomes
correction_rule a claim contradicted by measurement is REVISED toward what the measurement supports, not deleted
correction_rule the workload that produced a correction is recorded, because it predicts where the next correction will come from

registry_note the live atlas and the frozen canonical estate are two registries; a claim present in one and absent from the other is a registry gap, not an absent design
registry_note a claim may be simultaneously DORMANT in the atlas and VERIFIED_ON_DISK in the canonical estate

interaction lineage-gates-supersession
  source architecture-claim
  destination readiness-state
  relation supersession_constraint
  preserves the origin, reason and evidence of every prior claim across a revision
  drops any supersession justified only by recency
  forbidden_inference a later and more detailed description -> a superseding claim
